{
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Plane UV (0…1, centre ½) and time."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_rings",
        "position": {
          "x": 768,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1068
        },
        "text": "Exact ring SDFs (`abs(|p − c| − r) − thickness/2`): an outer double ring and one inner ring. A negative SDF is inside the line, so the *union* of several shapes is simply their minimum."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_sigils",
        "position": {
          "x": 768,
          "y": 864
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2292
        },
        "text": "A 5-point star and a triangle share the centre and rotate in opposite directions (`rotation = ± time × spin`, degrees). Filled-shape SDFs become outlines with `abs(sdf) − thickness`."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_runes",
        "position": {
          "x": 3264,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 4434
        },
        "text": "`polar.x` (turns) + `time × speed` is cut into *Rune Count* sectors: `id = floor(a × N)`, `local.x = fract(a × N)`, `local.y` = radius remapped from 0.29…0.39 to 0…1. Three hashes of the sector id give three points `0.15 + 0.7·h`; the rune is the segment A–B, the segment B–C and a fixed vertical stem — a different glyph for every sector. The result (in rune-cell units) is scaled by 0.1 to world units."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_merge",
        "position": {
          "x": 7902,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2990
        },
        "text": "One SDF for the whole sigil (`min` of everything). *Line* = anti-aliased coverage (`sdfMask`, 1.5 px). *Glow* = `(1 − max(sdf, 0) / size)²` — a quadratic falloff — modulated by a slow `sin` pulse. Both fade out towards the plane's edge so the quad never shows."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_color",
        "position": {
          "x": 11096,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "`colour = (line colour × line + glow colour × glow) × edge fade`; alpha = saturate(line + glow) × edge fade."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 12454,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Additive blend, ZWrite off, two-sided."
      }
    ],
